Subject: ecm: retain inner VLAN headers above bridge access ports

On NSS kernels vlan_dev_real_dev() walks through every VLAN upper. Use the
immediate lower device to apply bridge-port stripping only to the VLAN that
is directly above the bridge. Inner QinQ tags remain on the wire even when
they use the same VID as the stripped outer VLAN.

Pack retained tags into the first available rule slot. Interface hierarchy
counts include stripped VLAN devices and must not leave a secondary tag
without a primary tag. Apply this to all four NSS IPv4/IPv6 frontends.

--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -364,7 +364,10 @@
 		return -1;
 	}
 
-	real_dev = vlan_dev_real_dev(vlan_dev);
+	/* Only the VLAN directly above the bridge is stripped on an access port.
+	 * vlan_dev_real_dev() skips intermediate VLAN devices on NSS kernels.
+	 */
+	real_dev = vlan_dev_next_dev(vlan_dev);
 	vid = vlan_dev_vlan_id(vlan_dev);
 
 	if (!netif_is_bridge_master(real_dev) || !br_vlan_enabled(real_dev)) {
--- a/frontends/nss/ecm_nss_ported_ipv4.c
